sequenceDiagram
  participant P as pipeline<br/>suffix routing
  participant H as hj-fastcgi handler
  participant Pool as bounded pool<br/>(maxConns, one acquisition deadline)
  participant A as FastCGI app<br/>(externally supervised, TCP or uds://)
  P->>H: validated script target (beneath docroot, regular file, access checks passed)
  H->>H: build CGI params — server-derived, HTTP_* validated, protected names not overridable
  H->>H: buffer request body under the shared budget (exact STDIN length)
  H->>Pool: acquire — poisoned by default
  Pool->>A: BEGIN_REQUEST · PARAMS (≤65,535 B records) · STDIN · empty terminators
  A-->>H: STDOUT: strict CGI head (CRLF only, one Status, Location default) + streamed body
  A-->>H: STDERR — byte-capped, control-escaped → error log, never to client
  A-->>H: END_REQUEST (exact 8-byte body)
  H->>Pool: clean END_REQUEST → mark reusable — anything else → poison + close
  H-->>P: response (hop-by-hop fields rejected)
